---
import DocLayout from '../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
import LegalIntro from '../components/LegalIntro.astro';
import Fact from '../components/Fact.astro';
import EmailLink from '../components/EmailLink.astro';
import Operator from '../components/Operator.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const toc = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', label: '1. Who we are' },
  { id: 'scope', label: '2. Scope and our roles' },
  { id: 'account', label: '3. Account and billing information' },
  { id: 'connected-accounts', label: '4. Connected Pages and accounts' },
  { id: 'messages', label: '5. Messages and attachments' },
  { id: 'ai', label: '6. AI and the knowledge base' },
  { id: 'purposes', label: '7. Purposes and legal bases' },
  { id: 'providers', label: '8. Service providers' },
  { id: 'storage', label: '9. Storage, security, transfers' },
  { id: 'retention', label: '10. Retention and deletion' },
  { id: 'disconnecting', label: '11. Disconnecting' },
  { id: 'rights', label: '12. Your rights' },
  { id: 'cookies', label: '13. Cookies and analytics' },
  { id: 'children', label: '14. Children' },
  { id: 'changes', label: '15. Changes to this policy' },
];
const c = site.commitments;
const l = site.legal;
---

<DocLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Get Assist collects, uses, shares, stores and deletes personal data, including messages from connected Facebook Pages and Instagram accounts."
  toc={toc}
>
  <div slot="intro">
    <LegalIntro title="Privacy Policy">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Summary in plain language</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate">
        <li>
          Businesses use {site.brand} to manage customer conversations, coordinate their team and
          use AI-assisted replies.
        </li>
        <li>
          For their customers’ messages we act on the business’s instructions. The business decides
          what is collected and how it is used.
        </li>
        <li>
          If a workspace turns on AI features, relevant message content is sent to the AI provider
          that workspace chose, so it can suggest or write a reply.
        </li>
        {c.noSellingData && <li>We do not sell customer data.</li>}
        <li>
          You can disconnect a Page or account at any time and ask us to delete data. See our{' '}
          <a href="/data-deletion">data deletion page</a>.
        </li>
        <li>This website sets no cookies and uses no analytics.</li>
      </ul>
    </LegalIntro>
  </div>

  <h2 id="who-we-are">1. Who we are and how to contact us</h2>
  <p>
    <Operator /> In this policy “we” and “us” mean the operator of {site.brand}.
  </p>
  <p>
    For any privacy question or request, email <EmailLink email={site.emails.privacy} />. For
    anything else, email <EmailLink email={site.emails.general} />.
  </p>

  <h2 id="scope">2. Scope and our roles</h2>
  <p>
    This policy covers the website at {site.domain} and the {site.brand} service.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>We decide how data is used (controller)</strong> for visitors to this website and for
      people who hold a {site.brand} account, such as account owners and their teammates.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>We process data on a business’s instructions (processor)</strong> for the
      conversations that business handles in {site.brand}. When a business connects its Facebook
      Page or Instagram account, the messages its customers send are processed for that business.
      The business is responsible for telling its own customers how their data is used.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="account">3. Account and billing information</h2>
  <p>When you create and use a {site.brand} account we process:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name, email address and sign-in credentials;</li>
    <li>the names, email addresses and roles of teammates you invite;</li>
    <li>workspace and project settings you choose;</li>
    <li>
      billing details needed to charge for the service, where a paid plan applies. Payment provider:{' '}
      <Fact fact={l.paymentProvider} />
    </li>
    <li>technical logs such as sign-in times and IP addresses, used to keep the service secure.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="connected-accounts">4. Data from connected Facebook Pages and Instagram accounts</h2>
  <p>When a business connects a Facebook Page or Instagram professional account, we receive:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the identifiers and names of the Pages or accounts selected;</li>
    <li>
      an access token issued by Meta that lets {site.brand} receive and send messages for those
      Pages or accounts;
    </li>
    <li>basic profile information of the person who connected the account, such as their name.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The permissions are listed on the <a href="/integrations/facebook">Messenger</a> and{' '}
    <a href="/integrations/instagram">Instagram</a> integration pages. We use this data only to
    provide the messaging features the business turned on.
  </p>

  <h2 id="messages">5. Message content, customer identifiers and attachments</h2>
  <p>For each conversation on a connected Page or account we process:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the text of messages sent and received;</li>
    <li>
      the identifier Meta assigns to the person messaging the business for that Page or account, and
      the name or username Meta shares with it;
    </li>
    <li>attachments such as images or files sent in the conversation;</li>
    <li>notes, assignments and handover details the business’s team adds.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="ai">6. AI processing and the knowledge base</h2>
  <p>
    Businesses add information to a knowledge base, such as answers, policies and product details.
    Where a workspace turns on AI features, relevant message content and knowledge base entries are
    sent to the AI provider and model that the workspace selected or configured, which returns a
    suggested or automatic reply.
  </p>
  <p>
    <Fact fact={l.aiProviderPolicy} />
  </p>
  <p>
    AI replies can be wrong, and a person on the business’s team can take over a conversation. More
    detail is on our <a href="/ai-transparency">AI transparency page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="purposes">7. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Providing the service</strong> to account holders (performance of our contract with
      you).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Processing customer conversations</strong> on the business’s instructions (as a
      processor; the business determines its own legal basis).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Security, fraud prevention and keeping the service working</strong> (our legitimate
      interests).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Billing and record-keeping</strong> (performance of contract and legal obligations).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Answering your messages to us</strong> (our legitimate interest in responding to you).
    </li>
  </ul>
  {c.noSellingData && (
    <p>
      We do not sell customer conversation data, and we do not disclose it to unrelated third
      parties for resale.
    </p>
  )}

  <h2 id="providers">8. Service providers and subprocessors</h2>
  <p>
    We process information to deliver the services our customers request. To do that we rely on
    hosting, communication and other service providers that are necessary to run the platform, and
    we share personal data with them only as needed for the purposes above. Our current list is on
    the <a href="/subprocessors">subprocessors page</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Some services are independent platforms rather than our subprocessors: Meta, which carries
    messages between a business and its customers, and the AI provider a workspace chooses for
    itself. Their own terms and privacy policies apply. We may also disclose data where the law
    requires it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="storage">9. Storage location, security and international transfers</h2>
  <p>
    Where data is stored: <Fact fact={l.storageLocation} />
  </p>
  <p>
    How we protect it: <Fact fact={l.securityMeasures} />
    {c.encryptionInTransit && ' Data is encrypted in transit.'}
    {c.encryptionAtRest && ' Data is encrypted at rest.'}
  </p>
  <p>
    International transfers: <Fact fact={l.transferSafeguards} />
  </p>
  <p>
    More detail is on our <a href="/security">security page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="retention">10. Retention and deletion</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Conversation messages: <Fact fact={site.retention.messages} />
    </li>
    <li>
      Account data after a customer stops using {site.brand}: <Fact fact={site.retention.account} />
    </li>
    <li>
      Logs: <Fact fact={site.retention.logs} />
    </li>
    <li>
      Backups: <Fact fact={site.retention.backups} />
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    An authorised workspace owner can ask for deletion at any time, including before these periods
    end. The <a href="/data-deletion">data deletion page</a> explains how.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disconnecting">11. Disconnecting and revoking access</h2>
  <p>
    A business can disconnect a Page or Instagram account inside {site.brand}, or remove{' '}
    {site.brand} in its Facebook or Instagram settings. After that we no longer receive new messages
    for it. Disconnecting is not the same as deleting: what happens to stored data is explained on
    the <a href="/data-deletion">data deletion page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rights">12. Your rights and how to use them</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct, delete or export your
    personal data, to object to or restrict some processing, and to withdraw consent. To use these
    rights, email <EmailLink email={site.emails.privacy} />.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you messaged a business that uses {site.brand}, that business is responsible for your
    conversation data. You can contact the business directly, or contact us and we will pass your
    request to it.
  </p>
  <p>You may also complain to the data protection authority where you live, if there is one.</p>

  <h2 id="cookies">13. Cookies and analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This website ({site.domain}) sets no cookies, runs no analytics and loads no third-party scripts
    or fonts. Cookies used by the {site.brand} app are listed on our{' '}
    <a href="/cookies">cookies page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="children">14. Children</h2>
  <p>
    {site.brand} is a service for businesses and is not directed at children.{' '}
    <Fact fact={l.eligibility} />
  </p>

  <h2 id="changes">15. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    If we change this policy we will update the “last updated” date above. If the changes are
    significant we will also tell account holders by email or in the app before they take effect.
  </p>
</DocLayout>
